## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design edge routing with policy-driven gating and cross-DC deployment, plus observability and security concerns in docker-dca.

## Key Concepts

- TLS termination at the edge with Nginx
- Central policy engine (OPA) integration
- Per-tenant feature flag evaluation
- Cross-DC routing semantics
- Observability with Prometheus and OTEL

## Code Example

```rego
package featureflag.allow
default allow = false
allow {
  input.tenant == "tenant-A"
  input.flag == "new_feature"
}
```

```nginx
# Nginx map-based routing example
http {
  map $http_x_feature_flag $upstream {
    default http://api_v1;
    "new_feature" http://api_v2;
  }
  server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    location /api/ { proxy_pass $upstream; }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you implement cache invalidation for policy decisions?
- How would you test the canary routing?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to configure a lightweight canary in a real swarm, using Traefik as a modern edge proxy, and integrate observability with OpenTelemetry. It checks practical networking, TLS setup, and traffic shaping without requiring complex multi-cluster setups.

## Key Concepts

- Docker Swarm overlay networks and service deployment
- Traefik ACME TLS with staging
- Weighted canary routing and health-check-based rollback
- Lightweight OpenTelemetry tracing (export to stdout) and header propagation

## Code Example

